.\" Man page for mrknwordle4
.TH WORDLE4 6 "2026-09-23" "mrknwordle4 4.1" "Games"
.SH NAME
wordle4 \- configurable terminal Wordle game
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wordle4
.RI [ OPTION ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wordle4
is an interactive terminal implementation of Wordle.  It loads its runtime
configuration and resources from the current working directory, then provides
game, dictionary, history, user, and plugin interfaces.
.PP
The interface requires a terminal of at least 80 columns by 25 rows.  Smaller
terminals display a resize prompt until they are large enough.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \--help
Display a short usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-a, \--about
Display program information and license text, then exit.
.TP
.B \-v, \--version
Display the program name and version, then exit.
.SH FILES
All paths below are resolved relative to the current working directory.
.TP
.B config.json
Required runtime configuration file.  It must use schema version 2.
.TP
.B core.json
Required core resource manifest.
.TP
.B accept.dict
Generated dictionary of accepted words.
.TP
.B answer.dict
Generated dictionary of possible answers.
.TP
.B i18n/
Localization catalogs.
.TP
.B user.db
Persistent user database, created on first successful initialization.
.TP
.B logs/
Diagnostic logs, created after normal startup initialization.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WORDLE_BACKEND
Override the configured terminal backend.  Supported values are
.BR auto ,
.BR curses , and
.BR ansi
on supported builds, plus the supported Windows backends.
.TP
.B PDC_LINES
Set the initial number of rows used by PDCurses.  If neither PDC_LINES nor
PDC_COLS is set, wordle4 requests the application default of 25 rows.
.TP
.B PDC_COLS
Set the initial number of columns used by PDCurses.  If neither PDC_LINES nor
PDC_COLS is set, wordle4 requests the application default of 80 columns.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful completion, including informational options.
.TP
.B 1
Startup or runtime error.
.TP
.B 2
Command-line usage error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Start the game from a prepared runtime directory:
.EX
cd /path/to/wordle4-runtime
wordle4
.EE
.TP
Use the ANSI backend explicitly:
.EX
WORDLE_BACKEND=ansi wordle4
.EE
.TP
Set a PDCurses window size explicitly:
.EX
PDC_COLS=80 PDC_LINES=25 wordle4
.EE
.SH NOTES
The PDCurses X11 backend requires an X core font that matches its configured
Unicode fixed font.  If the font is installed in a directory not present in
the X server font path, add it and refresh the path before starting wordle4,
for example:
.EX
xset +fp /usr/share/fonts/misc
xset fp rehash
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xset (1)
